# Testing conventions

- pytest with `asyncio_mode = auto` — write `async def test_...` directly,
  no `@pytest.mark.asyncio` needed.
- `tests/unit/` must run without a database. Anything needing Postgres goes in
  `tests/integration/` (gated by `INTEGRATION_TESTS=1`).
- Every functional change ships with a test. Normalization changes get a
  before/after case in `tests/unit/test_normalization.py`.
- Mirror existing file names: `test_<module>.py` matching the `src/core/<area>`
  it covers (`test_clustering.py`, `test_compare.py`, `test_evidence.py`, …).

```bash
make test-unit                        # fast, no DB
pytest tests/unit/test_clustering.py -v   # single file
make test-int                         # needs: docker compose up postgres -d
```
